---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { legal } from "@/lib/legal";

const privacyMailto = `mailto:${legal.privacyEmail}`;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Notice"
  description={`Cookie Notice for ${legal.brandName}.`}
  heading="Cookie Notice"
  eyebrow="Cookies · TTDSG / ePrivacy"
>
  <p>
    This Cookie Notice explains how <strong>{legal.brandName}</strong> (
    {legal.legalName}) uses cookies and similar technologies on
    {legal.siteUrl} and related app routes. It supplements our
    <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored on your device. Similar technologies
    include local storage, session storage, and pixels. Under German TTDSG/TDDDG
    § 25, storing or accessing information on a terminal device generally
    requires consent, except where strictly necessary to provide a service you
    requested.
  </p>

  <h2>2. How we use cookies today</h2>
  <h3>2.1 Strictly necessary — authentication (Clerk)</h3>
  <p>
    To sign you in and keep your session secure, our authentication provider
    <strong>Clerk</strong> sets cookies / storage required for login, session
    continuity, CSRF protection, and related security (including optional bot
    challenges via Cloudflare as part of Clerk). These are necessary to provide
    the account areas you request and do not require consent under TTDSG/TDDDG §
    25(2).
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Category</th>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Duration (typical)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Strictly necessary</td>
        <td>Clerk</td>
        <td>Session, auth state, security</td>
        <td>Session / up to provider defaults (often months for “remember me”)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Strictly necessary</td>
        <td>DeclineGuard / host</td>
        <td>Security headers, load balancing, abuse prevention (may be cookie-less)</td>
        <td>As needed for request security</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>2.2 Preferences / functional</h3>
  <p>
    We may store non-essential UI preferences in local storage (e.g. dismissed
    tips). Where required, we will request consent before non-essential storage.
  </p>

  <h3>2.3 Analytics &amp; marketing</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not currently use advertising cookies or third-party
    analytics pixels</strong> (e.g. Google Analytics, Meta Pixel). If we add
    them, we will update this Notice, present a consent banner where required,
    and only set non-essential cookies after opt-in.
  </p>

  <h3>2.4 Google Fonts</h3>
  <p>
    Our site may load fonts from Google Fonts. Your browser may request font
    files from Google servers, which can involve transmission of your IP address
    to Google. If you require a fully local font setup, contact us — we can
    self-host fonts as a hardening step.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete or block cookies in your browser settings. Blocking strictly
    necessary auth cookies will prevent sign-in and dashboard use. For
    Google/Clerk account cookies, also review those providers’ settings.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Updates</h2>
  <p>
    We will revise this Notice when our cookie practices change. Last updated:
    {legal.lastUpdated}.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={privacyMailto}>{legal.privacyEmail}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
